'''6.''' A piece of soft iron applied simply by contact to the two poles of a magnet or electromagnet as a means of maintaining the magnetic power undiminished. {{smaller|In dynamo-electric machines (which see, under ''electric'') the armature is a cylinder or ring of laminated soft iron wound with coils of insulated copper wire. This armature is rotated rapidly in the field of the adjacent electromagnets. In the Holtz electric machine the armature is a strip of varnished paper attached to the edge of the openings or windows of the fixed plate. Also called ''armor''.}}

'''armazine''', ''n.'' See ''armozeen''.

